{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>The heads of the tribes.</b> In my opinion this pericope was after the war of Midian; therefore it is after it, like \"and Miriam and Aaron spoke against Moses\" being after \"and they were in Hazeroth,\" as I explained. And the verse says that the children of Gad came to Moses and to Eleazar and to the princes of the congregation, and it mentions their words, and afterward it is written, \"and Moses commanded them, Eleazar the priest and Joshua son of Nun and the heads of the fathers' tribes\" — they are the princes of the congregation mentioned. And because Moses said to the children of Gad and the children of Reuben, \"what proceeds from your mouth you shall do,\" therefore it is written, \"and Moses spoke to the heads of the tribes,\" and there it is written, \"according to all that proceeds from his mouth he shall do.\"" "<b>To the children of Israel.</b> That they should say thus to the children of Israel:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "Resolved והכ׳ as והכתוב, 'and the verse says'; the abbreviation is standard but the referent (Numbers 32:2 ff.) is confirmed by the flow of the argument."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:52.177105263Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}